# AGENTS.md - {{ project_name }}

Instructions for AI coding agents (open AGENTS.md format; `CLAUDE.md` imports this file). Keep it lean: link to the
docs that hold the detail, load them when the task needs them (progressive disclosure). A rule changes in its doc
first, then here.

## Hard rules

1. **Read before you design.** [`CONTEXT.md`](CONTEXT.md) (boundaries, owners), the lessons of the area you touch
   ([`docs/lessons.md`](docs/lessons.md)), and the issue's Done-when. Table and column names come from the schema
   reference or the migration files, never from memory.
2. **Trunk-based.** Branch from the latest `origin/{{ default_branch }}`, one PR per deliverable slice, squash merge
   after every check is green. Lanes work in worktrees under `.tmp-session/wt/`, never in the main checkout.
3. **Commits and PR titles** are `feat|fix|chore|refactor|docs|ci|test|perf: <description>`; the body carries
   `Refs {{ issue_key_prefix }}-<n>`. Never a closing keyword (`Fixes`, `Closes`): an issue is Done only when it is
   verified live ([`.claude/skills/project-ship/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/project-ship/SKILL.md)).
4. **Who ships.**
{%- if team_shape == 'lead-plus-agents' %} The orchestrator agent (the main session) pushes, merges after green CI,
   deploys and verifies live during the dev phase; risky classes (auth or permissions, migrations, CI or secrets, data
   deletion) get an independent agent review first. Subagents code and commit locally only (hook-enforced).
{%- elif team_shape == 'engineers-plus-agents' %} Engineers merge; agents code, test and commit locally, and a risky
   class (auth or permissions, migrations, CI or secrets, data deletion) needs a human reviewer as well as CI.
{%- else %} Engineers code, review and merge; every PR has a human reviewer.
{%- endif %}
   From the first production release or the first paying customer, the tech lead approves every infrastructure,
   migration, auth and data-deletion PR before merge (playbook gate G7).
5. **Thresholds are settings.** Every new threshold, limit, cap, quota, retry limit or retention window is read from
   the admin-editable settings registry with a seeded default (`docs/templates/settings-entry.md`), never a literal or
   an environment variable alone.
6. **Cost before paid.** Quote the monthly cost of any new paid service or paid run and get an explicit yes for that
   item first; paid batch runs go 3 items, then at most 50, then the rest
   ([`.claude/skills/project-batch-run/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/project-batch-run/SKILL.md)).
7. **No live identifiers in the repo.** No account ID, resource ID, ARN, secret value or personal data in code, docs
   or tests (`tools/resource_id_lint.py`, gitleaks). Test fixtures use invented names.
8. **Single-line cloud CLI commands** in docs and scripts (no backslash continuations).
9. **Tests come with the change**; run the targeted tests and `bash scripts/pre-push.sh` before you hand work back.
10. **Lessons.** When a mistake's root cause is found, write one principle with a Guard field
    ([`.claude/skills/project-lessons/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/project-lessons/SKILL.md)); a lesson a test can check
    becomes that test.

